{"id": "EUVD-2026-76524", "enisaUuid": "a895d91b-15fd-3830-94a3-808b2eed74cd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs: reject invalid MFT LCNs from boot sector\n\nThe NTFS boot sector stores the MFT and MFTMirr locations as unsigned\n64-bit LCNs, but parse_ntfs_boot_sector() decoded them into an s64.\n\nA crafted high-bit value could therefore become negative and pass\nthe existing upper-bound check. The invalid value then propagated into\nthe MFT zone allocator and could result in an out-of-bounds access to\nlcn_empty_bits_per_page.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:44", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f8420b68a6f05ca2b03779d8208814ec539b9e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc9d09fef78410bcd37ac05168cbd5f6dd75d3d2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v9qj-wpxr-47gc", "CVE-2026-89612"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.55, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3ec1b9ec-4f8b-37ea-bc88-843d3f4e23f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "48f85403-2739-3aaa-af32-4ad87b09697f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "4ff3501e-9081-372a-ad4c-3de0e367413f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "11ccc9107dc460de28af90fac1f42404d9802735 <cc9d09fef78410bcd37ac05168cbd5f6dd75d3d2"}, {"id": "573b618b-16e1-3247-9285-b933cd4f431b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "11ccc9107dc460de28af90fac1f42404d9802735 <8f8420b68a6f05ca2b03779d8208814ec539b9e5"}, {"id": "5878f3d9-489b-34b8-8213-bad7d90ac7c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "97de9485-2759-3753-840c-9a030f32dc47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"